    [Doc] Add nine Ascend recipe overlays for upstream migration (#19381)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Companion source PR for [recipes
    #1160](https://github.com/vllm-project/recipes/pull/1160). Add the
    Ascend recipe manifest, contributor/cutover guidance, upstream reusable
    validation workflow, and **nine** Huawei overlays already present in
    [vLLM at
    52a65d7b](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/tree/52a65d7b19e9e3ad86bf1e3b6954e4e11eeec7da/recipes/models):
    
    - Qwen3-30B-A3B, Qwen3.5-397B-A17B, Qwen3.6-27B, Qwen3.8-27B
    - DeepSeek-V4-Flash, DeepSeek-V4-Flash-Vision-Exp
    - Kimi-K3, GLM-5.3, GLM-5.3-Flash
    
    Each overlay links to its merged source. Qwen3.8 uses
    `guide_sections.ascend`, matching `<!-- overlay:vllm-ascend:ascend -->`
    in the companion vLLM split. MiniMax-H3, other Omni content, pending
    model PRs, and further tutorial migration are deferred.
    
    Follow #1160's staged cutover: merge the Ascend source first; register
    the official source in the renderer with identical-entry support while
    vLLM remains unsplit; merge the vLLM split; finally enable
    `scope.exclude_brands: [Huawei]` for vLLM. Update source locks to
    official commits during registration.
    
    CI uses the renderer's reusable `validate-recipes.yml@main`, temporarily
    pinned through `renderer-ref` to #1160's **unmerged preview**
    [9ffe8f5d](https://github.com/vllm-project/recipes/commit/9ffe8f5da08b1f2ae862464805ebc487529c34d4).
    Its vLLM base is the preview split
    [7846aee8](https://github.com/esmeetu/vllm/commit/7846aee877aa763108476ed035d410fe8e175bca);
    the validator replaces the Ascend source with this PR's files. Remove
    the preview pin once renderer main registers the official source with
    identical-entry support. No custom validator is included.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No runtime/API change or immediate change to published pages. Publishing
    requires the coordinated renderer/vLLM cutover above. Configuration
    values are preserved; after splitting, variant display order can change
    because overlay keys follow base keys, as noted in #1160. Scattered
    Ascend prose remains in the base guides for later migration.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Ran the unmodified upstream `node scripts/validate-source.mjs --source
    vllm-ascend --dir <this-repo>/recipes` in a disposable renderer checkout
    at `9ffe8f5d`: strict assembly of **215 models / 9 overlays**, schema
    validation and JSON API generation passed (**276 promoted variants**, 11
    existing collision warnings).
    - Verified all nine parsed overlays match #1160's example source
    `159363d`, and retain the merged vLLM source settings.
    - Checked the overlap stage against both merged source `52a65d7b` and
    the companion split's parent `b3047819`: applying the overlays leaves
    serialized recipe content and key order unchanged.
    - Checked split `7846aee8` plus these overlays against its matching
    parent `b3047819`: all nine reconstructed recipes are deeply equal,
    including GPU fields and guide text. Qwen3.8 fills its original Ascend
    marker before DFlash2/References, with no duplicated section or leftover
    marker. Kimi's base differs between `52a65d7b` and `b3047819`; these
    source-version changes are not attributed to the overlays.
    - Independent read-only review of the complete 12-file PR scope found no
    blocking issues.
    - `git diff --check`, Markdown lint, actionlint, codespell and typos
    passed. Required `bash format.sh ci` was rerun in an isolated Windows
    checkout: the available checks passed, but gitleaks/check-logger lacked
    `/bin/bash`, shellcheck was unavailable, and
    long-functions/symbolic-meta could not run `python3`. Current-head Linux
    CI is reported by the checks below.
    - Local renderer checks used Node 24.19; reusable CI uses Node 22. No
    new NPU inference/performance validation or browser preview was
    performed. Hardware verification labels are inherited source evidence.
    
